      "content": "That second version is a bit better, but honestly, the first one went completely off the rails with that weird gibberish at the end. I get that you're trying to hit the metric, but the description needs to actually make sense for an art gallery. \n\nLet's try another one. This one is a small, smooth, polished white marble sphere resting on a rough, weathered wooden base. It's about 15cm in diameter. \n\nThe app is really picky about the \"richness\" score though—if the score is too low, the piece won't even show up in the \"Featured Art\" section. Try to write a really high-scoring, descriptive paragraph for this one. Just please make sure it actually sounds like a real curator wrote it and doesn't just turn into a list of random words.",
